id: pm-web-i0td
title: Restyle every pm-web screen in the Triplicate brand and show live collaborator copies
description: "Companion phase: pm-cli-website-z2kf. Consume exact-commit pm-brand assets through a generated published directory; preserve a pixel-tested token migration commit, then apply the Triplicate field grammar across authentication, app views, legal pages, PWA assets and live arrivals from other authors. Validate fixture screenshots, keyboard access, AA contrast, reduced motion, npm and Bun release gates, packaging and an isolated image build."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-16T22:27:12.851Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-17T04:56:40.147Z"
author: codex-agent
comments[46]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-16T22:27:46.814Z",codex-agent,"Started isolated package work. Baseline main is 54c694b. Plan: fixture-only screenshots first; generated dev-only pm-brand asset pipeline and pixel comparison; Triplicate screens and accessible board; attributed live-copy arrivals; full unchanged release gates, packaging, isolated image build and PR evidence. Current brand main contains tokens only; optional fonts and icons will be consumed when available. Existing test PostgreSQL is reachable; hosted resources stay outside this work."
  "2026-10-16T22:40:05.742Z",codex-agent,"Asset-copy and immutable static-cache regressions pass 2/2. Behavioral revert: restoring only the original static middleware makes the published-brand cache assertion fail (expected no-cache, received public max-age=0); the function was restored afterward. Baseline evidence covers 108 fixture screenshots. Temporary exact legacy aliases isolate the first migration; the following restyle replaces them with the shared contract."
  "2026-10-16T22:40:44.720Z",codex-agent,"Migration pixel comparison passed 30/30 main-view images. Across 1440/768/390 and both themes: items, board baseline and open detail are identical (max delta 0). Sign-in max channel delta 27/255 with at most 28 changed pixels (0.00718% area); projects max 15/255 with at most 31 pixels (0.00795%). Sparse glyph-edge antialiasing only. Lint passes; duplication 0%; docstrings 706/706."
  "2026-10-16T22:59:16.767Z",codex-agent,"Restyle uses only shared contract aliases, installed self-hosted fonts and brand artwork, field underlines, real item strips, status shapes, a responsive board and in-flow cookie notices. Focused asset/legal/i18n/service-worker checks pass 41/41. The first keyboard matrix passed 108/108 basic audits; a stronger traversal exposed and fixed the graph canvas Tab trap. New brand commit 952a4bc includes fonts/icons/logo but its Git prepare assumes a checkout. Script-disabled installation retains those built assets; CI then runs this package prepare explicitly. When compiled tokens are absent, build output derives equivalent typed data from the installed CSS; compiled kit tokens take precedence when supplied. No shared thresholds or pinned SDK changed."
  "2026-10-16T23:02:36.832Z",codex-agent,"Stronger scripted checks now traverse every action, verify a focus ring, detect viewport overflow and compute painted text contrast including opacity. They found and fixed dim adjacent-month calendar dates. Seventeen requested screens passed these checks in the first light/desktop run. The remaining live-arrival traversal catches the existing SSE list replacement during focus traversal; the next signature commit will patch fields in place to remove that focus loss. Generated brand assets include the shared mark, all PWA icons and licensed font files; no generated files are tracked."
  "2026-10-16T23:46:50.417Z",codex-agent,"Live copies now patch readonly fields in place, keep comment and edit drafts and keyboard focus, suppress own account/session echoes, and retain the changed-field border for five seconds. Six browser scenarios cover the settle timing, blocked rose, polite announcements, own echoes, stale draft partial writes, stable comment entries and reduced motion. The real database SSE regression also verifies authenticated display names and the Project member fallback without trusting an author supplied in the edit body."
  "2026-10-16T23:48:33.538Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: replacing only emitItemEvent with its previous implementation makes the new real database SSE test fail because the payload lacks author: Editor. The changed function was restored. Existing itemId and userId remain unchanged; display-name lookup failure cannot fail an already committed edit. Initial quality checks pass with zero duplicate lines and all 737 declarations documented."
  "2026-10-17T00:07:37.104Z",codex-agent,"The first PM-linked collaboration run exceeded its 120-second runner budget. The 600-second retry exposed a pre-existing SSE test that started its five-second delivery timer before a real CLI write finished. It now uses the existing continuously reading wire helper and starts the unchanged five-second deadline after commit, with stricter item-id and actor-id assertions. No coverage, duplication or capacity threshold changed. The Docker build also exposed npm 10 Git-prepare behavior; the builder and CI now pin compatible npm 11.17.0. The image build passes and its tag was deleted."
  "2026-10-17T00:14:46.720Z",codex-agent,"The revised PM-linked collaboration command passes 12/12 with zero failures, skips or cancellations, including the real PostgreSQL/wire-SSE attribution regression. The pack dry run contains 330 files, including 34 generated brand files and all three self-hosted font files, icons, mark artwork and licenses; runtime Git dependencies: zero. The final matrix is being recaptured after sentence-case copy alignment. Local release checks will use the canonical fleet inventory; its two catalog assertions pass 2/2."
  "2026-10-17T00:39:23.882Z",codex-agent,"Implementation and fixture review are complete: 216 PNGs are published on pr-screenshots, with 300 keyboard/contrast/overflow audits, 8512 real Tab stops, 1917 painted text/background checks and 36 live scenarios. Both mobile themes were recaptured after correcting the inherited metadata column rule. Mid-arrival reduced-motion preference changes also restore source text immediately. Focused checks pass 41/41 and live collaboration 12/12; packed output includes 34 brand files and no runtime Git dependency. Full local release attempts hit the existing 300-second catalog-consumer deadline under contention; no deadline, coverage, duplication or capacity limit was relaxed. The existing CI jobs run both complete npm and Bun release commands with isolated Git identity; exact-head receipts will be reported in the PR. Canonical fleet assertions pass 2/2. Strict tracker health passes with its existing storage advisory retained."
  "2026-10-17T00:50:13.565Z",codex-agent,"PR 216 is open. CodeQL identified missing rate limiting on the fixture screenshot server filesystem handler. A global express-rate-limit middleware now bounds its loopback API and static routes. Type checking, lint and the unchanged zero-duplication gate pass for the fix. The production application and its token assets are unchanged by this test-tool fix. Full npm and Bun gates are running in the existing isolated CI matrix; local attempts retain the unchanged catalog-consumer deadline failures as non-acceptance evidence."
  "2026-10-17T00:59:26.800Z",codex-agent,"The isolated CI run completed 666 tests: 664 passed and two release-policy guards failed. The guards correctly rejected the extra global npm installs and npm_config_ignore_scripts in the publisher workflow. The fix removes those additions, retains its original npm 11.19.0 trusted publisher, and uses only the ignore-scripts CLI flag there. All eight release-policy tests now pass unchanged. A separate fresh-cache install with compatible npm succeeds without any ignore-scripts environment override. The ordinary build/CI npm pin remains scoped outside the publishing job. Prior CI coverage exceeded all unchanged floors: statements/lines 92.51%, branches 81.48%, functions 95.22% or 96.12% by Node runtime; the failed test run is not acceptance."
  "2026-10-17T01:15:10.068Z",codex-agent,"Both isolated npm release gates now pass all 666 tests with zero failures, skips or cancellations. Node 22 coverage is statements/lines 92.51%, branches 81.48%, functions 95.22%; Node 26 functions are 96.12% with the same other dimensions. Bun then exposed a Git-archive checksum mismatch during lock migration. Removing only the optional pm-brand packed-archive integrity entry preserves its exact commit and every registry checksum and resolution. A separate fresh-cache Bun install passes with integrity verification enabled. The isolated image build is checking npm against the same lockfile before the next exact-head CI run."
  "2026-10-17T01:18:07.870Z",codex-agent,The complete Node 22 image build also passes with the cross-runtime lockfile and its test image is removed. Fresh Bun and Docker npm both consume the unchanged exact kit commit. The feature remains in progress and is released for orchestrator review; full npm and Bun CI gates will rerun at the checksum-fix head. No hosted service or data was accessed.
  "2026-10-17T01:46:23.559Z",codex-agent,"Round 1 screenshot review: pin the final held kit, remove prepare and token-export workarounds, attach arrival captions to item sheets, replace the closed chip with its stamp, and group mobile secondary actions. Re-run npm and Bun release gates, browser audit, pack and image checks; refresh the screenshot matrix and PR #216. Main is already an ancestor of this branch."
  "2026-10-17T01:54:49.639Z",codex-agent,"The final kit installs with scripts enabled and exports tokens through its public entry. Removed the parser and prepare bypasses from build, CI, image, README and review notes. Canvas imports are bundled for the browser. Focused asset/contrast/live-value tests pass 9/9. Arrival slots are per sheet; closed detail status uses a single replaceable slot. Mobile secondary actions use a native disclosure with Escape focus return. Release gates use an isolated database on the disposable test service and isolated Git identity."
  "2026-10-17T01:57:10.214Z",codex-agent,"Normal image installation also runs pm-web own canonical merge-driver prepare, which needs tracker configuration and Git metadata. The builder now receives only the tracked settings/schema and initializes build-local Git before npm ci; runtime still installs production dependencies only. No lifecycle scripts are suppressed. The fresh Bun fixture requires the same initialized-clone preconditions."
  "2026-10-17T01:59:09.522Z",codex-agent,"Browser regression found the new board caption could enlarge the desktop card intrinsic width during arrival. Constrained the board item grid to minmax(0, 1fr), reserved two caption lines, and restarted the final screenshot matrix. Mobile light/dark already passed 112 audits and all lifecycle/arrival scenarios before this additional sizing fix. Geometry assertions remain exact."
  "2026-10-17T02:00:34.931Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: rebuilding with only caption targeting restored to the old modal-or-page selector makes BRAND_ACCEPTANCE=1 BRAND_QUICK=1 node scripts/brand-browser.ts fail: the affected row caption is empty instead of Updated by Alex just now. Rebuilding with only the closed-detail markup restored to chip plus stamp makes the same audit fail: one status-closed chip exists where zero is required. Both production functions were restored before final acceptance."
  "2026-10-17T02:02:59.715Z",codex-agent,"Final image build passes with the base npm 10 and scripts enabled; image removed. Pack dry run has 357 files, including 61 generated brand assets and all three fonts, and zero runtime Git dependencies. Fresh-cache Bun installation also passes with the exact lock integrity retained. Local Node 24 release coverage hit the known unchanged 300-second catalog fixture deadline; stopped the failed run and retrying the entire gate with the installed supported Node 26 runtime. No gate budget or threshold changed."
  "2026-10-17T02:04:11.256Z",codex-agent,"Removed the obsolete generated token-module URL from the service-worker precache list as the last token-export workaround. The browser palette bundle remains precached. The final 1440-pixel light/dark arrivals now pass exact card geometry checks for list, board and detail, including settled captions."
  "2026-10-17T02:07:48.822Z",codex-agent,"The complete first final matrix passes: 140 screenshots, 332 browser audits and six live scenario groups. Visual inspection then caught desktop board tags squeezed by the status chip in narrow columns. Stacked those two metadata fields inside the existing reserved slot and refreshing the matrix so published images include the last visual correction."
  "2026-10-17T02:10:39.521Z",codex-agent,"The unchanged catalog consumer fixture also exceeds its 300-second deadline on local Node 26 under host contention. Both failed npm attempts are retained as failures, with no acceptance claim. Running the full Bun command next. Full npm and Bun acceptance will be verified from the final-head GitHub CI matrix; unchanged budgets, coverage floors and zero-duplication gate remain required."
  "2026-10-17T02:14:51.588Z",codex-agent,"Reviewed round 1 matrix passes 140 fresh AFTER screenshots, 332 screen/tab audits, 9806 Tab stops, 2167 painted contrast pairs and 42 live-update cases. Preserves 108 original BEFORE frames; list/board/detail each have mid-animation and settled frames in every width/theme. Focused tests pass 9/9 plus service-worker tests 9/9; both behavioral reverts fail as expected and are restored. Pack has 357 files, 61 generated brand files, three fonts and zero runtime Git dependencies. Final Docker build and image removal pass. Implementation is ready for review; final-head npm/Bun CI results will be published in PR #216 and its pr-screenshots release-gates receipt. Releasing the implementation claim for orchestrator verification; item remains in progress."
  "2026-10-17T02:25:46.758Z",codex-agent,"Exact-head CI Node 26 passes its complete npm release gate, production audit, pack and packed consumers, then fails the Bun dependency-install check before the Bun release gate starts. Reclaimed the item to diagnose and repair this installation boundary without changing thresholds. Node 22 is still progressing."
  "2026-10-17T02:26:34.687Z",codex-agent,"CI identifies the npm-to-Bun Git archive checksum mismatch previously handled by this branch. Re-pinning regenerated the optional npm Git tarball checksum. Removing only that checksum restores archive-format portability while retaining the exact c64fb9da7937c2d239f67357cab325f6a9cff29a Git commit and every registry checksum. Scripts remain enabled, and no global integrity bypass is introduced. Reproducing npm-ci then fresh-cache Bun migration before and after the fix."
  "2026-10-17T02:35:54.186Z",codex-agent,"The guarded clean npm restore completed successfully with scripts enabled. A shell-guard error during isolated Bun setup interrupted the local Bun gate after both catalog scenarios passed; that interrupted run is not acceptance. Only expected source/tracker changes remained. Using the verified official Bun 1.4.3 binary, a clean npm install followed by fresh-cache Bun reproduces the exact CI IntegrityCheckFailed error with the optional Git archive checksum retained. Testing the corrected lock with another fresh cache now."
  "2026-10-17T02:36:30.991Z",codex-agent,"Bun 1.4.3 before/after migration proof passes: a clean npm install with the npm-generated Git archive checksum reproduces IntegrityCheckFailed; changing only that optional checksum entry and using a second fresh Bun cache installs successfully with scripts enabled. Clean package-worktree npm ci and all 18 focused asset/contrast/live/static tests pass after recovery. The corrected-lock Docker build and image removal also pass. Rendered sources and kit commit are unchanged, so all 140 reviewed screenshots and 332 audits remain applicable. Releasing the corrected implementation for final-head CI; source acceptance remains pending on the new matrix."
  "2026-10-17T03:06:25.599Z",codex-agent,"Round 2: verifying all six unresolved CodeRabbit threads against the current branch, then adding independently reverted behavioral regressions, compact inline arrival captions, closed-action evidence, the complete browser matrix and release/package/image gates. Review threads remain unresolved for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-17T03:09:41.253Z",codex-agent,All six review findings reproduce in current source. Round 2 reconciles authoritative list/board membership while reusing patched rows and preserving detail drafts/focus; closes direct-body graph dialogs by removal; names confirmation prompts; maps every contract status and neutral draft/custom graph nodes; preserves draw opacity; restores Delete access and explicit Reopen. Empty list captions now occupy no separate band. The current pm-brand main 952a4bc fails normal Git preparation because pm merge install sees no Git repository; the verified c64fb9d pin remains unchanged pending owner guidance. No dependency lifecycle is bypassed.
  "2026-10-17T03:13:10.364Z",codex-agent,"Verified the kit relationship: pinned c64fb9d is ten commits ahead of current main 952a4bc, with zero commits behind. Re-pinning would downgrade and remove the archive-safe preparation already accepted in round 1. Retaining the newer verified pin; no dependency changes or script bypasses. The first five behavioral revert probes failed as expected; final probes and the fresh full audit are in progress."
  "2026-10-17T03:14:07.978Z",codex-agent,"Independent rebuilt behavioral reverts: membership rollback times out waiting for the filtered row to leave; hideModal rollback leaves one graph dialog after Escape; confirmDialog rollback cannot find the named Delete item dialog; lifecycle rendering rollback fails contract styling; opacity rollback fails the expected faded drawing; disabling only the Close tab makes its Delete button unreachable; renderItemRow rollback reserves a 28px empty caption band. All seven probes exited 1 and production files were restored. The canvas probes are being refined to isolate the reviewed fill and label assignments exactly."
  "2026-10-17T03:15:58.032Z",codex-agent,"Final canvas revert evidence: restoring only the pre-fix lifecycle drawing makes the in-progress alias fill white (#ffffff) instead of contract canary wash (#fbf1c6). Restoring only changed opacity assignments makes the filtered drawing lose its 0.07 alpha. Both focused probes exit 1 against rebuilt production modules; all production source is restored. Full npm/Bun gates now run through the linked pm tests, and the requested six width/theme captures and isolated image build are underway."
  "2026-10-17T03:23:58.660Z",codex-agent,"The restored seven-case suite passes through pm test (exit 0). The 1440 and 390 width/theme matrices pass; 768 dark is finishing. Closed-sheet screenshots show Reopen, Delete item and Use as template with Start/Pause/Claim absent. The normal pack dry run contains 357 files, 61 generated brand files and three fonts, with zero runtime Git dependencies. The Node 22 Docker build passes and its test image is removed. Strict tracker health passes with the existing stale-work advisory. Full linked release gates remain running."
  "2026-10-17T03:24:56.741Z",codex-agent,"The complete six-combination browser matrix passes: 146 fresh AFTER screenshots, 338 screen/tab audits, 9866 real Tab stops, 2251 painted contrast-pair checks, 42 live-update cases and 42 reviewed regression cases. The 108 original BEFORE frames are preserved. Every requested list/arrival, board, closed detail, graph and confirmation frame is refreshed. Screenshot-branch artifacts are prepared; publication waits for the remaining release-gate results."
  "2026-10-17T03:44:25.585Z",codex-agent,"The local npm release gate returned exit 1 after the test/coverage phase. This is failed evidence, not acceptance. The linked runner buffers detailed per-command stdout until the selected batch completes, so the precise failure is pending while the full Bun gate runs. No threshold, timeout, coverage scope or fixture assertion has changed. The independent browser matrix, behavioral revert proofs, pack dry run and Docker build remain passing evidence."
  "2026-10-17T03:51:50.427Z",codex-agent,"Final action-scope correction: only Start, Pause and Claim are hidden for finished items, exactly as requested. Release remains available alongside Delete, Reopen, Use as template and Update. The browser regressions now assert Release visibility and availability; the complete fixture matrix is being refreshed for this final rule. Earlier notes that included Release in the hidden set are superseded."
  "2026-10-17T03:54:50.488Z",codex-agent,"The final Release rule is verified against a real scratch tracker using the pinned CLI: initialize, create, claim, close, then release succeeds. Restoring only the old Release-disabled branch fails the browser closed-action assertion (exit 1); the production function is restored and rebuilt. The restored linked browser regressions pass again, lint passes, zero duplication passes, and the final-rule pack and Docker build/removal pass. All six screenshot combinations are being recaptured."
  "2026-10-17T03:59:34.536Z",codex-agent,"Final-rule browser acceptance is complete across 1440/768/390 in light and dark: 146 fresh AFTER screenshots, 338 audits, 9872 real Tab stops, 2251 painted contrast-pair checks, 42 live-update cases and 42 reviewed regression cases. Eight independent behavioral revert probes fail as expected, including the supplemental Release availability rule. The 108 original BEFORE frames are preserved. These final counts supersede the earlier capture totals."
  "2026-10-17T04:01:07.783Z",codex-agent,"Visual verification caught a 390px overlap after preserving Release. The action row now wraps without shrinking its buttons. The shared finished-action assertion checks sheet bounds, text clipping and pairwise overlap. Reverting only the action-row CSS fails at 390px with the clipping assertion (exit 1); CSS is restored. This is the ninth independent behavioral revert probe. The matrix, pack and image are being refreshed for this final geometry fix."
  "2026-10-17T04:09:58.523Z",codex-agent,Membership reconciliation now retains the previous order of existing rows and appends newly matching rows. The membership regression reverses the authoritative fixture response during a title arrival and asserts stable row order and focus. Reverting only the order-preservation step fails with reversed row IDs (exit 1); production is restored and rebuilt. This tenth independent probe protects the original non-displacing arrival contract while status membership and board relocation remain covered.
  "2026-10-17T04:16:09.710Z",codex-agent,"Full local npm and Bun attempts each finished at 663/666 passed, 2 failed and 1 canceled, with zero skips/todos. Both reproduced the existing catalog 300-second deadline and subsequent spawn ENOTDIR, now enriched on pm-web-qdhx. npm additionally reproduced the tracked spawn-overlap ordering issue (pm-web-fhob); Bun exceeded the tracked graph read budget (pm-web-hqqp), 10691 versus 10000 ms. Coverage statements/lines were 91.76% and 92.01%, below the unchanged 92.07% floor. These attempts are failed evidence; final-head GitHub npm/Bun acceptance will be recorded separately in the linked PR and screenshot-branch release receipt."
  "2026-10-17T04:18:09.034Z",codex-agent,"Pre-push refresh found pm-brand main advanced to 7ad0970, two commits ahead of the previously tested c64fb9d pin. The comparison changes only release automation, its test/proof and kit tracker metadata; runtime assets are unchanged. Re-pinning to the new exact main commit with normal lifecycle scripts, then refreshing consumer/build/browser/image evidence. Complete npm and Bun release acceptance for the final pin will be taken from exact-head CI; the two earlier local attempts remain explicitly failed evidence."
  "2026-10-17T04:23:30.894Z",codex-agent,"The final exact-commit pin 7ad0970 installs with normal lifecycle scripts using Node 22 and npm 10; ignore-scripts is false and the root merge-driver preparation executes successfully. Only the three Git commit references change in package.json/package-lock.json. Every registry checksum is retained, with the existing optional Git archive checksum omission preserved for Bun compatibility. The kit comparison confirms unchanged runtime assets. Final validation is now on this pin."
  "2026-10-17T04:42:46.076Z",codex-agent,Final graph review preserves type/tag and facet/external outline colors while item status mode uses the exact lifecycle borders. The graph regression now exercises all three modes and lanes. Restoring only the unconditional status border fails the outline assertion. Unknown statuses also use a graphite fallback in initial/repaint color selection; the shared palette ignores inherited properties. Restoring only the palette guard fails on constructor-like status names with token.slice TypeError. These eleventh and twelfth behavioral probes are restored and rebuilt; final source hashes confirm no counterfactual survived.
  "2026-10-17T04:56:39.422Z",codex-agent,"Final round 2 source is restored after all 12 behavioral revert probes. Each independent revert failed as expected; final SHA-256 checks cover all eight production files. The complete final-pin matrix passes at 1440/768/390 in light and dark: 146 fresh AFTER PNGs, 338 screen/tab audits, 9872 Tab stops, 2251 painted contrast pairs, 42 live cases and 42 reviewed regression cases. Original 108 BEFORE frames remain intact. Visual inspection confirms the inline right-aligned arrival caption and compact unaffected rows, plus mobile closed Delete/Reopen with Start/Pause/Claim absent and no clipping/overlap. Linked pm regressions pass, focused tests pass 18/18, check/lint/docstrings pass, duplication is zero, clean npm ci runs preparation scripts, production audit passes, pack has 357 files/61 brand assets/3 fonts/no runtime Git dependency, and the final Docker build passes with its tag removed. Earlier local full npm/Bun failures remain recorded on pm-web-qdhx. Fresh exact-head CI acceptance and public screenshot/revert/package/release receipts will be attached to PR 216 and the pr-screenshots branch without changing the accepted source head. No thread state changes are authorized; replies follow the push."
